# @generated by `cargo buckal`
#
# (os, cpu) config_settings backing the refined keys of `os_deps` /
# `os_named_deps`. See `_platform_label` in `wrapper.bzl`.
#
# These live in the buckal cell rather than the consuming repo so that generated
# BUCK files are self-contained: a crate that needs `libc` only on aarch64 Linux
# must not require the repo to have hand-written the right `config_setting`.
#
# They deliberately overlap `prelude//os/constraints:*`. A dependency conditional
# on (arch, os) is emitted under the refined key, and Buck2's select refinement
# picks that branch over the bare OS branch because it constrains a strict
# superset. A platform must therefore declare a CPU constraint for the refined
# branch to be reachable — `prelude//platforms:default` does, deriving both OS
# and CPU from the host.

